      "judge": [
        {
          "check": "root-cause",
          "criterion": "root-cause@3",
          "input": "[BUG]\nAsking for next week's events makes event.list end with an error and a problem opens. The cause is that RANGE_RULES has no next_week entry, so rangeBounds reads undefined.offset and throws a TypeError. Asking for this week or all events still works.\nfiles: src/events.ts\n\n[TICKET_GOALS]\n1. Fix TypeError in event.list when range is \"next_week\": RANGE_RULES in src/events.ts has only this_week, so RANGE_RULES[range].offset throws (src/events.ts:40). Add next_week: {offset: 1}, and make unknown ranges not crash (reject with ToolRejection \"invalid_range\" and reportProblem named \"unknown_range\"). Failure branches to report: unknown_range (invalid input range), store_unavailable (existing). event.list is a read tool; keep its public contract.\n\n[EVIDENCE_FILES]\n(none)",
          "state": "judged",
          "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
          "verdict": "root_cause",
          "quote": "RANGE_RULES in src/events.ts has only this_week, so RANGE_RULES[range].offset throws (src/events.ts:40)",
